---
description: |
  Updates the TruePattern rule catalog from normalized Sigma rules.

  The catalog is a lookup table keyed by Sigma rule ID, the ID that detection
  findings of the `sigma` operator carry in `finding_info.analytic.uid`. Each
  entry holds the OCSF `osint` object of the rule, its license, and the full
  supplied rule text and external references, including attribution and
  notices. Rules without a Sigma rule ID get no entry.

  The operator expects the normalized output of
  `truepattern::sigma::update_rules`, which holds one rule per Sigma rule ID
  and matches the rule file. With other input, the last rule per Sigma rule ID
  wins.

  Declare the lookup table in your configuration. A `write-timeout` removes
  rules that leave the feed from the catalog:

  ```yaml
  # contexts/truepattern-sigma-rules.yaml
  type: lookup-table
  persist-interval: 5min
  write-timeout: 30d
  ```
args:
  named:
    - name: context_name
      type: string
      default: truepattern-sigma-rules
      description: Lookup-table context to update.
---

where @name == "ocsf.osint_inventory_info"
unroll osint
where osint.related_analytics[0].uid != null
// Sigma's parsed `policy.data` omits YAML comments. Keep the original text
// separately so findings retain notices that appear only in comments.
_rule_text = move osint.detection_pattern
// Choose a populated reference for the summary only; never filter the rule.
_license = unmapped.external_references?.where(ref =>
  ref.source_name == "rule-vendor-license"
  and (
    (ref.external_id?.trim() else "") != ""
    or (ref.url?.trim() else "") != ""
  )
).first()
context_update $context_name,
  key=osint.related_analytics[0].uid,
  value={
    osint: osint,
    rule_text: _rule_text,
    external_references: unmapped.external_references?,
    license: {name: _license.external_id?, url: _license.url?} if _license != null,
  }
